            <field name="html_content">
                &lt;h2&gt;Module 1: Risk Recognition and Site Readiness&lt;/h2&gt;
                &lt;p&gt;Before any emergency, a security guard must already know where people can be protected quickly and safely.&lt;/p&gt;

                &lt;h3&gt;Pre-Incident Project Mapping&lt;/h3&gt;
                &lt;ul&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;Identify safe areas: interior corridors and rooms away from windows.&lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;Mark dangerous zones: glass facades, exposed areas, and upper floors.&lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;Know all emergency exits and alternate stair routes.&lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;Know exact gas and electricity shutoff points for rapid utility isolation.&lt;/li&gt;
                &lt;/ul&gt;

                &lt;h3&gt;Emergency Kit Standards&lt;/h3&gt;
                &lt;ul&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;First aid kit for bleeding control and basic trauma support.&lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;Flashlight for low-visibility conditions and power failures.&lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;Backup battery or power bank for communications continuity.&lt;/li&gt;
                &lt;/ul&gt;

                &lt;h3&gt;Early Drone Attack Indicators&lt;/h3&gt;
                &lt;ul&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;A low buzzing sound similar to a small motorcycle.&lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;A drone with triangular wings flying at low altitude.&lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;Public reports from witnesses: treat all credible reports as urgent.&lt;/li&gt;
                &lt;/ul&gt;

                &lt;h3&gt;Activation Trigger&lt;/h3&gt;
                &lt;p&gt;If a warning sign is seen or heard, immediately begin protective procedures without delay.&lt;/p&gt;
            </field>
        </record>

