            <field name="html_content">
                &lt;h2&gt;Module 2: Civilian Protection and Crowd Control&lt;/h2&gt;
                &lt;p&gt;Curiosity during an aerial threat increases risk. The guard must quickly control movement and reduce group vulnerability.&lt;/p&gt;

                &lt;h3&gt;Immediate Public Control Rules&lt;/h3&gt;
                &lt;ul&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;Do not allow people to stop and watch the sky.&lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;Issue clear, firm instructions and move people without argument.&lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;Direct everyone immediately to designated safe areas.&lt;/li&gt;
                &lt;/ul&gt;

                &lt;h3&gt;Movement Strategy to Reduce Casualties&lt;/h3&gt;
                &lt;ul&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;Divide crowds into smaller separate groups so they do not become a single target.&lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;Move people at a side angle away from the drone's path.&lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;Guide people behind solid walls or any low ground.&lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;Keep everyone away from vehicles, fuel tanks, and power poles.&lt;/li&gt;
                &lt;/ul&gt;

                &lt;h3&gt;Priority Support Group&lt;/h3&gt;
                &lt;ul&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;Assist children and elderly first.&lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;Assign nearby adults to support people with reduced mobility.&lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;Keep communication calm and repetitive to prevent panic spread.&lt;/li&gt;
                &lt;/ul&gt;
            </field>
        </record>

