            <field name="html_content">
                &lt;h2&gt;Module 3: Blast Protection and Building Shelter&lt;/h2&gt;
                &lt;p&gt;When immediate shelter is limited, your instructions must be precise and physically demonstrated.&lt;/p&gt;

                &lt;h3&gt;No-Cover Emergency Body Position&lt;/h3&gt;
                &lt;p&gt;If no nearby cover exists, instruct and demonstrate:&lt;/p&gt;
                &lt;ol&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;Lie flat on your stomach.&lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;Point your feet toward the direction of the explosion.&lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;Cover your head and ears with your hands.&lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;Open your mouth slightly to reduce pressure-wave impact.&lt;/li&gt;
                &lt;/ol&gt;

                &lt;h3&gt;Building Interior Protection Rules&lt;/h3&gt;
                &lt;ul&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;Move everyone away from glass windows immediately.&lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;Use interior corridors and lower floors for cover.&lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;Use stairs only. Do not allow elevator use.&lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;Ask people to shelter under sturdy tables where available.&lt;/li&gt;
                &lt;/ul&gt;

                &lt;h3&gt;Successive Wave Discipline&lt;/h3&gt;
                &lt;ul&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;Stay alert. Attacks may come in successive waves.&lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;Do not allow people to leave shelter points too early.&lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;Wait for official authority clearance before release.&lt;/li&gt;
                &lt;/ul&gt;
            </field>
        </record>

