                &lt;h2&gt;Module 4: Casualty Care and Scene Control&lt;/h2&gt;
                &lt;p&gt;After immediate protection, the guard must stabilize injuries while controlling secondary risks.&lt;/p&gt;

                &lt;h3&gt;Immediate Injury Response&lt;/h3&gt;
                &lt;ul&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;If there are injuries, bring the first aid kit immediately.&lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;Request help from anyone with first aid experience.&lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;Prioritize stopping bleeding with direct pressure on wounds.&lt;/li&gt;
                &lt;/ul&gt;

                &lt;h3&gt;Debris and Hazard Discipline&lt;/h3&gt;
                &lt;ul&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;Do not allow anyone to touch debris or unexploded parts.&lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;Create a no-entry perimeter around suspicious remains.&lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;Preserve site condition for specialist authority handling.&lt;/li&gt;
                &lt;/ul&gt;

                &lt;h3&gt;Information Security&lt;/h3&gt;
                &lt;ul&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;Do not allow filming of strike locations.&lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;Instruct everyone not to share videos or tactical details.&lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;Control rumor spread by using one clear authorized message.&lt;/li&gt;
                &lt;/ul&gt;
            </field>
