                &lt;h2&gt;Module 5: Vehicle and Roadside Survival Procedures&lt;/h2&gt;
                &lt;p&gt;If explosions occur while driving, your decisions must prioritize immediate protection and hazard avoidance.&lt;/p&gt;

                &lt;h3&gt;While Driving During Explosions&lt;/h3&gt;
                &lt;ul&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;Slow down immediately and pull over safely to the side.&lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;Avoid bridges, power poles, and exposed utility structures.&lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;If a nearby building is available, enter and shelter inside.&lt;/li&gt;
                &lt;/ul&gt;

                &lt;h3&gt;Open Area Vehicle Shelter&lt;/h3&gt;
                &lt;ul&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;Remain inside the vehicle when no better shelter exists.&lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;Turn off the engine.&lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;Stay below the level of vehicle windows.&lt;/li&gt;
                &lt;/ul&gt;

                &lt;h3&gt;Final Professional Standard&lt;/h3&gt;
                &lt;p&gt;People usually follow the security guard. Stay calm, model correct behavior, and maintain strict procedure discipline until authorities confirm safety.&lt;/p&gt;
            </field>
